"""OnionPress tray app for Ubuntu / Linux desktops.

A thin presentation layer around the bash launcher: the widgets only.
Polls the daemon's state file (~/.onionpress/daemon-state.json, written
by `onionpress daemon`, the onionpress-daemon.service user unit since
#407; read through onionpress.daemon_client as the Mac menubar reads it) every 2
seconds and reflects state via the AppIndicator. Every action is `/opt/onionpress/onionpress <subcommand>`
run through the UIs' shared client (src/onionpress/ui_client.py, issue
#526: the Mac menubar runs the same code), so the headless / SSH-only
path remains the single source of truth.

The file deliberately stays one module — at ~700 lines it's easier to
audit and ship than a sprawling package. Split if it grows past 1000.
"""

